During validation, the duplicate appointment_id records did not follow one consistent financial pattern. We found cases with 2 billed rows and 2 non-null fee values, 1 billed row but 2 non-null fee values, 0 billed rows but 2 non-null fee values, and also 0 billed rows with both fee values null. Appointment 130789 was the simpler case, with 1 billed/non-null fee record and 1 null record.  
Because of these different patterns, a simple is_billed or non-null filter may not be sufficient for all appointments, which is why a dedicated staging layer may be useful once the session_cost definition is finalised.